synckit delta 1 complete: cc-sync/synckit-delta1 @ 2a201e3 (7072196 + review fix). It covers D4/D5/D8/D9/D10 plus explicit kinds, snapshot-only artifact changes and the CommitBatch durability restructure. Measured on this Mac: a 16384-object batch 148.2 s → 24.7 s (32768 F_FULLFSYNC → plain fsyncs + one barrier per level); a 32 MiB batch 0.30 s → 0.065 s.
The astra review found 4 real issues, each fixed with a failing-first test:
- BLOCKER: a digest reached both as a blob and as a manifest gave a false ACK, and GC could delete the live child. The walker now tracks the semantic kind reached, and Closure, Complete and GC marking share it.
- MAJOR: the peer reprobe bypassed live local policy; the local state is now sampled after the probe.
- MAJOR: supersede waited for the 10 s deadline; it now uses the dirty flag at each batch boundary, with a one-batch progress guarantee against livelock.
- The fourth finding was fixed as reported.
synckit final merge Run wf_1a000879-e5b (task #11), in worktree /Users/yasyf/.claude/worktrees/synckit/delivery on branch cc-sync/artifact-delivery:
- merge delta1 into ea6d2df, reconciling the overlapping fixes into one implementation that passes the union of both test sets;
- accepted pins bounded to prior-acked ∪ current;
- Store Open syncs object dirs;
- full gates + commit measurement;
- a whole-diff astra review with 2 lenses (delivery assurance; transfer safety/durability/bounds), then a fix pass;
- CHANGELOG v0.40.0 + reference docs written via a codex/astra prose lane with writing-docs, checked with slop-cop.
